Fix the nyquist and loop-tempo-estimator sources for clang/MinGW

Two more muse_deps recipe patches, for pinned sources compiled in:
- xlisp.h aliases _setjmp to setjmp with an object-like macro. mingw-w64's
  setjmp() is itself a macro expanding to the two-argument _setjmp(), and
  clang then resolves the call to its one-argument _setjmp builtin
  ("too many arguments"). Function-like aliases expand the same way
  everywhere else.
- LteDsp.h uses std::vector without including <vector>; libc++'s
  <functional> does not pull it in.

diff --git a/muse_deps/recipes/loop-tempo-estimator/patch/0001-include-vector.patch b/muse_deps/recipes/loop-tempo-estimator/patch/0001-include-vector.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..11cf6e9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/muse_deps/recipes/loop-tempo-estimator/patch/0001-include-vector.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+LteDsp.h: include <vector> for std::vector
+
+The header relies on <functional> pulling in <vector>, which MSVC's and
+libstdc++'s do but libc++'s does not.
+
+diff --git a/source/LteDsp.h b/source/LteDsp.h
+--- a/source/LteDsp.h
++++ b/source/LteDsp.h
+@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
+ #pragma once
+ 
+ #include <functional>
++#include <vector>
+ 
+ namespace LTE
+ {
